### attendance-service on your PC (Lab 4) - start it first:  cd services/attendance-service && npm run dev
### Open in VS Code with the REST Client extension and click "Send Request".
### For requests that need a token: sign in with identity/requests.http first and paste the accessToken.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3004
@token = PASTE-ACCESS-TOKEN-HERE

### Health -> 200, runtime pc
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

@classId = PASTE-A-classId

### My reliability (strikes, suspension, attendance rate) as a member -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reliability/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Check in with the 6-digit code from the trainer -> 201 (400 wrong code, 403 NOT_BOOKED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/attendance/{{classId}}/check-in
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "123456" }

### Attendance sheet as the trainer of the class -> 200 (403 for other trainers)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/attendance/{{classId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Audit log as admin -> 200 (403 for everyone else)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit?day=2026-11-25
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Internal endpoint without the service key -> 403 INTERNAL_ONLY
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/members/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/eligibility
